"The prognosis is driven by several concerning factors, including a preoperative PSA of 190 and positive surgical margins with seminal vesicle invasion. The pathological findings indicate an advanced local disease burden, evidenced by the presence of lymphovascular invasion and documented lymph node metastasis. A countervailing finding is the ISUP grade group 2 diagnosis from the prostatectomy specimen, which is lower than the Gleason 4+3 seen on biopsy. Furthermore, the nodal status was sampled, providing a definitive assessment rather than widening uncertainty due to missing sampling. The postoperative PSA trajectory remains unknown, and this information would significantly revise the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 34.46 months. This is a predicted recurrence horizon, not evidence of observed recurrence. The sensitivity range is 25.85–43.08 months; its coverage has not been validated."
